title "The fundamental theorem of calculus"
layout layered dir=down
page a3
font 8pt..36pt wrap=17em

style input color=#1565C0
style operation color=#EF6C00
style result color=#2E7D32

node function "Function f(x)" .input
| quantity changing over an interval
| continuity and integrability control which theorems apply
node limit "Limit" .operation
| f(x) approaches L as x approaches a
| epsilon-delta definition makes the claim precise
node derivative "Derivative f'(x)" .operation
| instantaneous rate of change
| f'(a) = lim h->0 (f(a+h)-f(a))/h
node tangent "Tangent line" .result
| local linear approximation
| y = f(a) + f'(a)(x-a)
node integral "Definite integral" .operation
| accumulated signed area
| limit of sums of rectangle areas
node antiderivative "Antiderivative F(x)" .operation
| F'(x) = f(x)
| any two antiderivatives differ by a constant
node theorem "Fundamental theorem" .result
| integral from a to b of f(x) dx
| = F(b) - F(a)
| continuity of f is a sufficient hypothesis
node area "Net accumulation" .result
| total effect across an interval
| signed area can cancel positive and negative parts
node mean "Mean value theorem" .result
| f continuous on [a,b], differentiable inside
| some c has f'(c) = (f(b)-f(a))/(b-a)
node substitution "Substitution" .result
| u = g(x), du = g'(x) dx
| reverses the chain rule inside an integral
node parts "Integration by parts" .result
| integral u dv = uv - integral v du
| reverses the product rule
node series "Power series" .result
| radius of convergence controls termwise operations
| Taylor remainder measures approximation error
node caution "Hypotheses matter" .result
| discontinuities can break naive FTC statements
| derivative zero implies constant only on an interval

function -> derivative
function -> integral
function -> limit
derivative -> tangent
integral -> area
antiderivative -> theorem
function -> antiderivative
area -> theorem
theorem -> antiderivative
function -> mean
integral -> substitution
integral -> parts
function -> series
limit -> derivative
theorem -> caution
mean -> caution

require function at top
require theorem at bottom
prefer tangent near derivative within=14em weight=2
prefer caution near theorem within=18em weight=2
